<Project>
  <!--
    Keep the net8 probe's NuGet artifacts OUT of the shared obj\ folder. BaseIntermediateOutputPath
    set inside an SDK-style csproj is too late for NuGet (MSB3539): the SDK import at the top of the
    file has already fixed where restore writes, so obj\project.assets.json is produced anyway - with
    net8.0 in it - and the LEGACY "CNC Core.csproj" then trips over it:

        Your project does not reference ".NETFramework,Version=v4.6.2" framework. Add a reference to
        ".NETFramework,Version=v4.6.2" in the "TargetFrameworks" property of your project file and
        then re-run NuGet restore.

    which is what VS Code's language server reported on every project reload (2026-09-20). Note that
    CNC.Core.net8.csproj DID set BaseIntermediateOutputPath in its body and obj\net8probe\ exists -
    so the redirect works for build intermediates and silently does not for restore. That is the trap:
    the folder being there looks like the problem is already solved.

    Unlike the sibling probes, this one's legacy project DOES carry a PackageReference
    (System.Text.Json), so its own restore overwrites the poisoned file and the app still builds -
    the two just take turns clobbering each other, and whichever ran last is what the IDE sees.

    Same fix as CNC Common, CNC Contracts, CNC Client and CNC Svg (see those folders' copies). This
    folder was the one that never got it.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(MSBuildProjectFile)' == 'CNC.Core.net8.csproj'">
    <MSBuildProjectExtensionsPath>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)obj\net8probe\</MSBuildProjectExtensionsPath>
    <BaseIntermediateOutputPath>obj\net8probe\</BaseIntermediateOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
